<title>USA: Miles Homes says gets federal court order.</title>
<headline>Miles Homes says gets federal court order.</headline>
<dateline>CHESHIRE, Conn. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Miles Homes inc said on Monday it obtained federal court orders to prohibit three of its former executives from using the company's trade secrets to begin a competing business.</p>
<p>Defendants Paul Vogel, David Gaither and Ray Parker allegedly contemplated a home-building venture which would use misappropriated proprietary information and trade secrets to compete unfairly with Miles Homes, the company said in a statement.</p>
</text>
